# Raw data and every derived cache: all of it is regenerated by the pipeline in README.md,
# and none of it belongs in git (the two pickles are ~280 MB each, the raw .psv tree ~313 MB).
datasets/training/
datasets/*.pkl
datasets/*.npz
datasets/*.log
datasets/robots.txt

# Notebook snapshots taken before each round of edits
EDA/*.ipynb.bak*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Tables and figures are small and worth committing, so they are NOT ignored:
#   EDA/*.csv, EDA/*.png, model/batch_effect*.csv, model/batch_effect.png

# the 8 MB model input is small enough to ship, so the pipeline can be run without the
# 313 MB raw download; the two ~280 MB pickles stay out (GitHub rejects files over 100 MB)
!datasets/physionet2019_model_input.npz
